    {
      "call_source": "transcript_item",
      "params_digest": "9d78de7d85c5891e",
      "query": "{\"content\": \"Distributed once so far for the September 28, 2026 conference. Expect no further relists before a decision; the United States waived its right to respond, indicating the government does not consider the petition to warrant the Court's review or view it as a significant circuit split on the Rule 52(a) standard of review for historical documents. Because the United States is already a party and the respondent, the Court will not call for the views of the Solicitor General (a CVSG). \\n",
